    "['mpls ldp remote-peer [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [0, 2], 'trans_command': 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5]', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]'}]]": 1,
    "['remote-ip [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-2/0/0.0 neighbor 192.168.3.3', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ldp interface ge-2/0/0.0 neighbor 192.168.3.3\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `remote-ip` command under `mpls ldp` context specifies an LDP neighbor address. In Juniper, this is equivalent to configuring an LDP neighbor under the protocols hierarchy. The command sets up LDP peering with the specified neighbor IP address (192.168.3.3 in this case) on the specified interface (ge-2/0/0.0 in this example, which corresponds to Huawei's GigabitEthernet2/0/0 interface from the original config).\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface ge-2/0/0.0 neighbor 192.168.3.3'}]]": 1,
    "['controller e1 [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/1\\n##  \\n\\nNote:  \\n1. Juniper uses dashes (-) instead of slashes (/) in interface naming  \\n2. The \"controller\" concept in Huawei maps directly to physical interface configuration in Juniper  \\n3. Additional E1 parameters would be configured under this interface hierarchy in Juniper, similar to how channel-set and other parameters are configured in Huawei\\'s controller mode', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1'}]]": 1,
    "['using ce1', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1 encapsulation ce1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/1 encapsulation ce1\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 encapsulation ce1\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent of \"using ce1\" (which sets the E1 controller to use CE1 framing in Huawei) would be configuring the encapsulation as \"ce1\" under the E1 interface. Since the original configuration applies this to both E1 controllers (1/0/1 and 1/0/2), both commands are included in the translation. The Juniper interface naming convention uses a hyphen (e1-1/0/1) instead of a space (e1 1/0/1).', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1 encapsulation ce1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 encapsulation ce1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/1 encapsulation ce1\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 encapsulation ce1\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent of \"using ce1\" (which sets the E1 controller to use CE1 framing in Huawei) would be configuring the encapsulation as \"ce1\" under the E1 interface. Since the original configuration applies this to both E1 controllers (1/0/1 and 1/0/2), both commands are included in the translation. The Juniper interface naming convention uses a hyphen (e1-1/0/1) instead of a space (e1 1/0/1).', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 encapsulation ce1'}]]": 1,
    "['frame-format [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1 framing crc4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for `frame-format crc4`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/1 framing crc4\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would need to specify this framing parameter for each E1 controller interface separately, hence the two commands for the two E1 controllers in the original configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1 framing crc4'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for `frame-format crc4`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/1 framing crc4\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would need to specify this framing parameter for each E1 controller interface separately, hence the two commands for the two E1 controllers in the original configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4'}]]": 1,
    "['channel-set [parameter1] timeslot-list [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ce1-1/0/1 channel 1 timeslots 1-31', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for `channel-set 1 timeslot-list 1-31`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ce1-1/0/1 channel 1 timeslots 1-31\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different interface naming convention (`ce1-1/0/1` instead of `e1 1/0/1`)\\n2. The command structure is different but achieves the same result - configuring timeslots 1-31 for channel 1 on the E1 controller interface\\n3. In Juniper, this would typically be part of the hierarchical configuration under the E1 interface settings\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ce1-1/0/1 channel 1 timeslots 1-31'}]]": 1,
    "['undo shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'unit [parameter2] disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]'}]]": 5,
    "['controller e1 [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent for the HUAWEI `controller e1 1/0/2` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 channelized timeslots 1-31\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 no shutdown\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different interface naming convention (`e1-1/0/2` instead of `e1 1/0/2`)\\n2. The CE1 configuration is implied by using the E1 interface type in Juniper\\n3. The commands are split into separate statements for framing, timeslots, and administrative state\\n4. The channel-set functionality is achieved through the `channelized timeslots` command\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 channelized timeslots 1-31', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 channelized timeslots 1-31', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent for the HUAWEI `controller e1 1/0/2` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 channelized timeslots 1-31\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 no shutdown\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different interface naming convention (`e1-1/0/2` instead of `e1 1/0/2`)\\n2. The CE1 configuration is implied by using the E1 interface type in Juniper\\n3. The commands are split into separate statements for framing, timeslots, and administrative state\\n4. The channel-set functionality is achieved through the `channelized timeslots` command\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 channelized timeslots 1-31'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 no shutdown', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 no shutdown', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent for the HUAWEI `controller e1 1/0/2` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 channelized timeslots 1-31\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 no shutdown\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses a different interface naming convention (`e1-1/0/2` instead of `e1 1/0/2`)\\n2. The CE1 configuration is implied by using the E1 interface type in Juniper\\n3. The commands are split into separate statements for framing, timeslots, and administrative state\\n4. The channel-set functionality is achieved through the `channelized timeslots` command\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 no shutdown'}]]": 1,
    "['using ce1', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set controllers e1 1/0/1 mode ce1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset controllers e1 1/0/1 mode ce1\\nset controllers e1 1/0/2 mode ce1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Huawei `using ce1` command configures the E1 controller to operate in CE1 (Channelized E1) mode.\\n2. In Juniper, this is translated to `set controllers e1 <interface> mode ce1` syntax.\\n3. Since the Huawei configuration applies this to both E1 controllers (1/0/1 and 1/0/2), both Juniper commands are included in the translation.', 'trans_template': 'set controllers e1 1/0/1 mode ce1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set controllers e1 1/0/2 mode ce1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset controllers e1 1/0/1 mode ce1\\nset controllers e1 1/0/2 mode ce1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Huawei `using ce1` command configures the E1 controller to operate in CE1 (Channelized E1) mode.\\n2. In Juniper, this is translated to `set controllers e1 <interface> mode ce1` syntax.\\n3. Since the Huawei configuration applies this to both E1 controllers (1/0/1 and 1/0/2), both Juniper commands are included in the translation.', 'trans_template': 'set controllers e1 1/0/2 mode ce1'}]]": 1,
    "['frame-format [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'framing crc4', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nframing crc4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: In Juniper, the command to set the framing format to CRC4 for E1/T1 controllers is `framing crc4`, which is the equivalent of Huawei's `frame-format crc4`. The functionality remains the same - it configures the cyclic redundancy check (CRC) framing type for error detection.\", 'trans_template': 'framing crc4'}]]": 1,
    "['channel-set [parameter1] timeslot-list [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `channel-set` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/1 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"channel-group\" instead of \"channel-set\"\\n2. The interface naming follows Juniper\\'s format (e1-1/0/1 instead of e1 1/0/1)\\n3. The timeslot-list parameter becomes \"timeslots\"\\n4. Both E1 controllers from the original config are included since they had identical channel-set configurations', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/1 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 framing crc4', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `channel-set` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/1 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/2 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"channel-group\" instead of \"channel-set\"\\n2. The interface naming follows Juniper\\'s format (e1-1/0/1 instead of e1 1/0/1)\\n3. The timeslot-list parameter becomes \"timeslots\"\\n4. Both E1 controllers from the original config are included since they had identical channel-set configurations', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/2 channel-group 1 timeslots 1-31'}]]": 1,
